# The build needs the two packages, the frontend, the ui-kit, the suites and
# dependencies.txt. Everything else only slows the context transfer down, and
# some of it would poison the image: a .venv built for another path, or a
# node_modules built for another platform.
#
# This stays at the repository root while the Dockerfile lives in docker/,
# because Docker reads the ignore list from the root of the build context and
# the context is the repository.

.devcontainer/
.git/
.github/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.py[cod]
**/node_modules/
build/
docs/
files/
frontend/dist/
output/
packages/gauntlet/src/gauntlet/web_dist/
tmp/
